messages:
emma_ops: FYI customer on Dedicated seeing repeated 422 SchemaError from fn.invoke. Error text: \"additionalProperties not allowed: \u2018target\u2019\". Happened after billing rollout.

raj_support: Can you paste the payload they sent + the exact timestamp/log id? Also which runtime version?

emma_ops: log_id=log_2024-11-02_08:42:17, runtime=redwood-dedicated-1.4.2, customer says their app sends a \"target\" object to hint routing. Payload below (redacted):

```json
{
  "fn": "charge_customer",
  "args": {
    "amount": 1999,
    "currency": "USD",
    "description": "monthly plan"
  },
  "target": {
    "endpoint": "payments-prod",
    "region": "us-west-2"
  }
}
```

emma_ops: The API returns 422 with body: `{\"error\": \"validation_failed\", \"details\": \"additionalProperties: 'target'\"}`

oliver_engineer: Thanks. Schema for fn.invoke expects top-level keys: fn (string), args (object), and optional metadata (object). It explicitly disallows additionalProperties. In 1.5.x we started enforcing strict schema to avoid silent routing hacks. Customer is sending \"target\" which is treated as an unexpected key.

raj_support: Short-term: can we recommend a payload transform they can apply? Suggest moving target into metadata.tool_hint or metadata.routing_hint.

oliver_engineer: Yep. Minimal repro curl to demonstrate server rejection: 

```bash
curl -sS -X POST https://api.redwood.example/v1/fn.invoke \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer REDACT' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{\"fn\":\"charge_customer\",\"args\":{\"amount\":1999,\"currency\":\"USD\"},\"target\":{\"endpoint\":\"payments-prod\"}}'
```

oliver_engineer: That will 422. Workaround payload that works: move target under metadata: 

```json
{
  "fn": "charge_customer",
  "args": {...},
  "metadata": {"routing_hint": {"endpoint": "payments-prod"}}
}
```

emma_ops: Customer is on Private (VPC) and their SDK historically allowed passing \"target\" and we had a shim in older runtimes that stripped it. That shim was removed in 1.5.0. They upgraded infra recently and hit this.

raj_support: Can we patch gateway to accept \"target\" again? If not, we need clear docs + a small compatibility shim for them.

oliver_engineer: Two options: 1) short-term: gateway middleware to map \"target\" -> metadata.routing_hint before validation (low risk). 2) long-term: change client SDK to stop sending \"target\". I'll open a tiny revertable patch for the shim and post the PR.

ci-bot: Build pipeline queued for branch fix/shim-target-map #PR-4721. Tests include fn.invoke schema compatibility tests.

emma_ops: Customer is ok with a short-term shim while they update SDK (they said they can ship in 2 weeks). Can you prioritize the patch?

oliver_engineer: I'll push the shim to canary infra and report back. Patch will: strip unknown top-level keys named \"target\" and move contents into metadata.routing_hint; log a compatibility warning; rate-limit logs to avoid noise. Example Node middleware: 

```js
function compatibilityShim(req, res, next) {
  const body = req.body || {};
  if (body.target) {
    req.body.metadata = req.body.metadata || {};
    req.body.metadata.routing_hint = body.target;
    delete req.body.target;
    console.warn('compat: migrated top-level target -> metadata.routing_hint');
  }
  next();
}
```
oliver_engineer: Will deploy to dedicated-canary in ~30m and follow up with rollout notes.

raj_support: Great. tagging @eng-oncall to watch for any regressions during canary.

emma_ops: Thanks team — I told the customer we have a short-term fix and SDK guidance. I'll share the repro and curl snippet with them. :thumbsup:
